                <pb facs="0830" n="710" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg710"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4397: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Harbin</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hanson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-30T17:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">May 30, 1922—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:54 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>It appears that Wu Pei-fu’s adherents gaining control North Manchuria. Local
                    Chinese military insist that Japanese aiding mutineers. Reported local Chinese
                    merchants favor Wu.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
